Week 3 Task 1

In the CampusEats project the client's mid project request to add a feature allowing a single order 
to be split across multiple resteraunts adds a large disruption to a traditional waterfall process.
Requirements, design and implementation are locked behind each other, meaning change would require 
extensive rework. The requirement document has to be updated and re approved, the design such as UI
demos and data models would need reworked, and finally completed code would need to be modified
and retested. Each stage of development would need new documentation, and more work leading to higher
costs and schedule delays.

On the otherhand, if the team were working in two week agile increments, the change would be absorbed
smoothly. The new feature would be added to the backlog, and prioritised during sprint planning. 
Constant integration and testing would rule out issues early, and client feedback could be incorporated
on a regular basis. Altogether the agile approach reduces the amolunt of reworking and cost while 
keeping its flexibility and involving characteristics.
